ok - capped and uncapped stale same-id retries publish their replacement
ok - failed stale-record removal prevents capped and uncapped replacement
ok - a listed window keeps its record, and that record holds the place against its own id and the next one
ok - an inventory read that omits the window removes the record and admits the next id
ok - a Herdr kill that returns without closing the pane keeps the record and the place
ok - a project with no declared capacity keeps today's uncapped dispatch
ok - a spawn is admitted while its project still has a free place
ok - a spawn beyond capacity is deferred before any record, brief, endpoint, worktree, or backlog move exists
ok - a project name with spaces is declared by taking the capacity from the last field
ok - a project name beginning with # is declared, and a # comment stays a comment
ok - a home reached through a symlink counts each of its workers once
ok - a recorded PR handoff or a cleanup each frees exactly one place
ok - a restart of a task id does not count that task's own record
ok - only this project's ship and scout records hold places
ok - a released-copy record holds a place only while its agent is alive
ok - an exited record frees its place unless a process still works in its worktree
ok - a dead record with a missing worktree keeps its place
ok - a live agent keeps its place
ok - every local home shares one declared capacity per project origin, and remote homes do not count
ok - an unreadable state directory or task record refuses admission rather than undercounting
ok - concurrent spawns can never both take the last place
ok - a spawn that fails after admission leaves no record and holds no place
ok - an unreadable declaration refuses every fresh spawn rather than guessing the limit
ok - a batch reports a capacity deferral as deferred, not failed
not ok - an Orca spawn ignored a held project lock: error: another spawn or cleanup holds the shared project lock for /tmp/fm-project-capacity.aWsufh/orca/project; refusing to race its capacity admission: expected exit 1, got 75
